# Rust / Cargo
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
# contracts/Cargo.lock IS committed on purpose: soroban-env-host declares an
# unbounded `ed25519-dalek = ">=2.0.0"` requirement, so an uncommitted lock
# lets cargo resolve a newer, incompatible major version and break the build
# (see contracts/Cargo.toml for the pin). Ignore any other Cargo.lock, e.g.
# under packages/, where a lockfile isn't meant to be committed.
Cargo.lock
!/contracts/Cargo.lock

# Go
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
go.work
vendor/

# Node / JavaScript
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
dist/
build/
coverage/
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local

# Environment variables
.env
*.env
!.env.example

